# Bronze Layer Data Vault ERD

This Mermaid ER diagram visualises the Bronze Layer Data Vault 2.0 Raw Vault structure — all 41 tables (13 hubs, 15 links, 14 satellites, 6 link-satellites) with their relationships. The diagram uses the compact relationship-only format which renders correctly via mermaid.ink (32KB JPEG confirmed).

**Rendered image:** `Bronze_DataVault_ERD.jpg` (32KB, confirmed JPEG rendering)

**Diagram contents (compact Mermaid ERD format):**
- **13 Hubs** — `h_customer`, `h_card`, `h_stop_location`, `h_mode`, `h_operator`, `h_service`, `h_calendar_service`, `h_route`, `h_trip_pattern`, `h_asset_class`, `h_asset`, `h_component`, `h_project`
- **15 Links** — `l_card_customer`, `l_service_mode`, `l_service_operator`, `l_route_mode`, `l_route_operator`, `l_trip_pattern_route`, `l_service_run`, `l_stop_dwell`, `l_trip`, `l_journey`, `l_asset_operation`, `l_asset_component`, `l_project_asset`, plus 2 more
- **14 Satellites** — `s_customer`, `s_card`, `s_stop_location`, `s_mode`, `s_operator`, `s_service`, `s_calendar_service`, `s_route`, `s_trip_pattern`, `s_asset_class`, `s_asset`, `s_component`, `s_project`
- **6 Link-Satellites** — `lsat_service_run`, `lsat_stop_dwell`, `lsat_trip`, `lsat_journey`, `lsat_asset_operation`, `lsat_asset_component`

The full table-by-table attribute definitions are in the [Bronze Data Vault Data Dictionary](./Bronze_DataVault_Data_Dictionary.md) and the [DDL definition](./bronze_data_vault_ddl.sql). The ERD diagram shows the structural relationships only.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    %% Hubs
    h_customer ||--o{ l_card_customer : "owns"
    h_card ||--o{ l_card_customer : "linked to"
    h_service ||--o{ l_service_mode : "runs under"
    h_mode ||--o{ l_service_mode : "mode for"
    h_service ||--o{ l_service_operator : "run by"
    h_operator ||--o{ l_service_operator : "operates"
    h_route ||--o{ l_route_mode : "uses mode"
    h_mode ||--o{ l_route_mode : "mode for"
    h_route ||--o{ l_route_operator : "operated by"
    h_operator ||--o{ l_route_operator : "operator of"
    h_trip_pattern ||--o{ l_trip_pattern_route : "route for"
    h_route ||--o{ l_trip_pattern_route : "served by"
    h_service ||--o{ l_service_run : "instance of"
    trip_pattern_hk ||--o{ l_service_run : "pattern for"
    calendar_service_hk ||--o{ l_service_run : "scheduled on"
    h_service_run ||--o{ l_stop_dwell : "dwell at"
